{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/111919?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A111919"}, "id": "111919", "updated": "2023-10-03T08:05:43.612039+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "109", "artid": "210", "year": 1977, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214855"}, "page_start": "210", "journal_title": "Annals Phys."}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Joglekar, Satish D."}], "texkeys": ["Joglekar:1976pe"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We study the operator product expansion of two gauge-invariant currents. We discuss the operators that may appear in the expansion. We study the hadronic matrix elements of gauge-variant operators that may appear in the operator product expansion and show that in the physical applications contemplated so far their hadronic physical matrix elements either vanish or cannot be isolated from strong interactions. We also study the gauge dependence of the Green's functions of the product of two (weak or e.m.) currents and show that is corresponds to the gauge dependence of the additional renormalization counterterms due to weak and electromagnetic interactions."}], "control_number": 111919, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0003-4916(77)90170-1"}], "titles": [{"title": "Local Operator Products in Gauge Theories. 2."}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "created": "1976-11-01T00:00:00+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Annals%20Phys.%2C109%2C210&size=3&page=1&fields=c